  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "en",
      "_type": "object",
      "value": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000001",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "b0nukxk0weep",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Exploring "
            },
            {
              "_key": "inug3zb3kuw7",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "w37penscleu7"
              ],
              "text": "Edfu"
            },
            {
              "_key": "y92ucnwzd3c9",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ": Navigating an Ancient Egyptian Town"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "w37penscleu7",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58841",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000002",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "In the heart of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000004",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000003"
              ],
              "text": "Egypt"
            },
            {
              "_key": "tbda4qbhi1wl",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", between the storied cities of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "2jzyen3krl6g",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "j4itcubgm5u1"
              ],
              "text": "Luxor"
            },
            {
              "_key": "nm9ol4d9da1g",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " and "
            },
            {
              "_key": "he6we2cbaqcj",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "docy95on5q85"
              ],
              "text": "Aswan"
            },
            {
              "_key": "dxn6a49psi16",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", lies Edfu, a town that gracefully balances the ancient and the modern. This charming locale, though small, is steeped in history and offers a uniquely intimate way to experience the rhythm of life along the Nile."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000003",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egypt",
              "newTab": true
            },
            {
              "_key": "j4itcubgm5u1",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            },
            {
              "_key": "docy95on5q85",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000b",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000007",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Transportation in "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000009",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000008"
              ],
              "text": "Edfu"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", much like the town itself, is a blend of simplicity and tradition. The ‘Kabouts’, local minibuses, are the lifeline of Edfu’s transport system. These modest yet efficient vehicles connect the town from the bustling train station to the myriad corners of its streets. Boarding a Kabout offers not just a ride, but an immersion into the daily lives of the townspeople. For a few Egyptian pounds, one can join the locals in their daily commutes, observing the vibrant street life through the window of a bus filled with the buzz of conversation and the warmth of community."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000008",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/edfu-travel-guide/weather-planning/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/edfu/edfu-seasonal-guide",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000010",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "These minibuses provide an unadorned yet authentic glimpse into Edfu. Each route taken by a Kabout is like a thread in the rich tapestry of the town, weaving past markets brimming with local produce, ancient structures standing as silent sentinels of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000000d"
              ],
              "text": "history"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", and the ever-present, life-giving Nile."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000d",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/the-worlds-first-labour-strike/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/blog/kiroku-ni-nokoru-saiko-kyu-no-rodo-sutoraiki",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001b",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000011",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "For those seeking a more leisurely and picturesque way to "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000013",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000012"
              ],
              "text": "explore"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000014",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " Edfu, horse-drawn carriages offer a timeless alternative. This mode of transport is a throwback to a bygone era and is available not just in Edfu but throughout the towns between Luxor and "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000016",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000015"
              ],
              "text": "Aswan"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000017",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ". A horse carriage ride in Edfu is not merely a means to an end but a "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000019",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000018"
              ],
              "text": "journey back in time"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ". The gentle clop-clop of the horse’s hooves on cobblestone streets, the slow pace allowing for the absorption of every detail, and the open-air view create a romantic and nostalgic experience."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000012",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/nuweiba-travel-guide/exploring/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://travel2egypt.org/nuweiba-travel-guide/exploring/",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000015",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/aswan-travel-guide/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/aswan",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000018",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/rosetta-rasheed-travel-guide/journey-through-time/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://travel2egypt.org/rosetta-rasheed-travel-guide/journey-through-time/",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001d",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The carriages, often ornately decorated, are piloted by drivers who possess intimate knowledge of Edfu’s streets and stories. As the carriage ambles along, one can observe the town’s rhythm, from children playing in the narrow alleys to vendors selling their wares. The driver might point out landmarks or share tales that have been passed down through generations, adding depth and color to the experience."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000025",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Edfu, home to the magnificent "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000020",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000001f"
              ],
              "text": "Temple of Horus"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000021",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", is a treasure trove of history. The Kabouts and horse carriages offer different lenses through which visitors can view this history, blending in with the local life, and experiencing the town’s "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000023",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000022"
              ],
              "text": "culture"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000024",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " and heritage in a manner that is both personal and profound."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001f",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/edfu-travel-guide/edfu-temple/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/edfu/edfu-temple",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000022",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/animals-in-ancient-egypt/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/blog/animales-en-el-antiguo-egipto",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000002a",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000026",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "In Edfu, the journey is as enriching as the destination. Whether you are navigating its streets in a bustling Kabout or taking in the sights at the leisurely pace of a horse-drawn carriage, you are part of a living history, a continuum of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000028",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000027"
              ],
              "text": "tradition and modernity"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000029",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " that is uniquely Egyptian."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000027",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/al-fayoum-travel-guide/stay-traditional-modern/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://travel2egypt.org/al-fayoum-travel-guide/stay-traditional-modern/",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
